// Wilderland Tool & Materials Library catalog (/tools/, /guides/tools/).
// The starting list for a project-based K–8 nature school, built from the categories community tool libraries and K–12
// makerspaces stock (MIT Edgerton Center's K–12 maker list, the Makerspace Playbook, library-of-things lists), shaped
// for Wilderland: outdoors in Eden, Utah, Life Skills challenges, Projects, Labs. Not an inventory yet: `have` is what
// we know we own (the items Alex listed on Nov 26, 2026); everything else starts at 0 ("not in the library yet") until a
// guide counts it in Inventory. What a guide sets in Inventory (Firestore toolInventory/{id}) overrides these numbers.
//
// Fields: id, n name, c category, k kind (tool | machine: stays put, book a time | material: take what you need),
//   have = how many we own, want = how many a school our size should have (for the shopping list),
//   a = who can borrow it:  open  any student
//                           badge a student who passed this tool's safety certification (tools/certs.js: one
//                                 certification covers a group of similar tools)
//                           guide only with a guide right there
//                           staff guides use it; students help and watch
//   No tool is limited by grade (Nov 27, 2026): the library is Upper Campus only (2–8), and certification decides who
//   can borrow on their own. loan = how long (day: back by the end of the day,
//   week: a project week, place: stays where it is, book a time; take: a material, nothing to return),
//   e = emoji, d = what it's for, m = make and model (when it matters), tip = care or safety.
